# The engine this product ships, pinned by tag and by content.
#
# `release.yml` downloads these two binaries from the engine repository's
# release of that tag and REFUSES to package anything whose SHA256 is not the
# one written here. The hashes come from the SHA256SUMS-engine that the
# engine's own workflow publishes next to the binaries — the ones that passed
# its customs (clippy, tests, the no-listener sweep) on BOTH platforms.
#
# Moving to a new engine is: tag it there, wait for its release, copy the tag
# and the two hashes here, one commit. `git log` on this file IS the history
# of which engine every Kanpachi release carried.
#
# A developer machine never reads this file: local builds keep coming from
# `Resolve-KanpachiEngine` (newest of C:\kt\release and friends), which is
# what makes iterating on the engine not require a release per attempt.
tag v0.1.2
sha256-windows 30708dd86d343d3c526f743ae135cec2f6aac36b80bc7e9ed1f3fdf442f59f3c
sha256-linux d82631ea3c59fb9bafafed5ec4e4802079f1ec7623cbce7092f78056f6c5812b
